  "hypothesis": "H-K1-2 (CTWS-2D): Combining corrected multi-depth Verduzco potential-field tilt-angle zero-crossing worms (B02/B03/B05/B09/B11/B15/B17), full-footprint USGS 3DEP 10 m piedmont-toe concave flexure & Perron-Royden drainage chi-knickpoints, BLM epithermal lode corridors, playa-detrended 222Rn U/Th, 8-azimuth 2-D multi-scale lineament context (CTX-2D), and strictly fold-visible multi-scale bend/two-host en-echelon relay anatomy allocated under a coupled 300 m CELF submodular objective with a >=52% far-field basin floor significantly outperforms 1-pixel point GBDTs (H-K1-1 & BASE_35) across both continuous/relay and detached blind fault populations.",
  "mechanism": "Subvertical basement fault steps produce depth-invariant potential-field tilt zero-crossings (theta = arctan(VDR/THDR) = 0; Verduzco et al. 2004) and sedimentary cover thickness jumps (||grad(B15)||) beneath flat valley fill, while transient footwall uplift preserves 10 m drainage chi-knickpoints and piedmont-toe concave hinges long after surface scarps diffuse; simultaneously, fracture mechanics concentrates secondary off-catalogue splays in restraining/releasing fault bends and overlapping two-host en-echelon relay ramps (Curewitz & Karson 1997; Faulds & Hinz 2015).",
  "mimic_process": "Pleistocene Lake Lahontan highstand (~1,334 m ASL) wave-cut shorelines, un-faulted >22 deg degraded bedrock facet crags, incised alluvial fan channel banks (LiDAR cross_max), TIGER road prisms, Tertiary dike swarms, and closed-basin playa uranyl-evaporite sinks (Carson/Humboldt Sinks); suppressed via explicit 1,334 m shoreline/crag/road gating, cross_max subtraction, playa evaporite detrending, and 2-D multi-scale linearity.",
